"A deepening is a trial period in which two knights entangle their lives toward a pairing."
"Partners are ideally of equal authority strength, usually young knights raised together."
"When the pairing becomes unbreakable and strengthening effortless, it is celebrated as esvulgivnas."
"Paired knights hold each other's spot in reality, lend authority and share skills in some ways."
"The profoundest pairs can hold each other away from death until healing is found."
"Pairing helps with affixation and allows limited mind reading at potentially any distance."
"It is painful, healers cannot aid it, and it was unknown to the early knights."
"A good partner is open, welcoming another's authority, and charming, touching it without discomfort."
"'Isn't satisfied with her own skill' is knight euphemism for a serious, possibly deadly affixation crisis."
"A knight hiding such a crisis may be removed from the squad until stable, to the Rapport or older squads."
"To complete a bond the power gap must close: one partner waits while the other speeds up."
"Most benefits of a bond come only after it is complete; deepening reveals each partner's skill fully."
